  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe part-alignment refusal in `setup_align::generation_problem` said \"an aligned part is not supported yet on a lathe or mill-turn machine\" for every non-mill setup, including sinker and wire EDM. It now names the setup's actual kind through `stock_sim::machine_kind_name`, the table #1229's `carry_machine_refusal` reads. The refusal condition is unchanged (same strictness; only the words change). The `setup_stock.rs` doc comment that said \"a lathe or mill-turn machine\" now says \"a machine that is not a mill\".\n\nEffort: low\nStacked on #1229 (issue/1182-carry-refusal-kind); retarget to main once #1229 merges.\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning test: `setup_align::an_aligned_setup_on_an_edm_names_the_edm_kind_it_is_refused_on` (sinker and wire EDM fixtures) - passes.\n- Suites run: setup_align (10), carried_fixtures_cache (7), lathe_workholding_kinds (10, 1 ignored), lathe_workholding_mill_post (3), setup_stock_source (8), rest_across_setups (7), setup_carry (9) - all green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` - green (app suites, 117 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` - clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The plasma and mill-turn wording through the alignment refusal (same helper; the mill-turn carry wording is pinned by the existing lathe/mill-turn test).\n- Full batch tier.\n\nChangelog: Part-alignment refusal names the setup's machine kind (sinker EDM, wire EDM, ...) instead of \"a lathe or mill-turn machine\" (#1230)\n\nFixes #1230\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
